{"id":"81baab4dfbca52e0184af6c66e2d4c8db4aa6387","axis":"silent","repo":"phan/phan","sha":"81baab4dfbca52e0184af6c66e2d4c8db4aa6387","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"NEWS.md","lines":["@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ Performance improvements:"," - In the `'balanced'` `process_file_assignment`, also try splitting groups of files weighing more than half or a quarter of an even share (not only more than a whole share) and use the partition with the lowest predicted maximum load: a large class hierarchy that is under a share but placed first no longer leaves one analysis process noticeably heavier than the others (on a large codebase with `--processes 4`, the heaviest worker went from ~25 % above the mean to a few percent)"," "," Bug fixes:","+- Fix `PhanParamTooManyInternal` being reported for every call with arguments to 58 internal methods and functions that the PHP 8.2, 8.3 and 8.5 signature deltas listed with their return type only: the `Random\\Randomizer` methods (`getBytes`, `getInt`, `pickArrayKeys`, `shuffleArray`, `shuffleBytes`), the `__unserialize` methods of the date, `SplFixedArray` and random engine classes, `Random\\Engine\\PcgOneseq128XslRr64::jump`, the PHP 8.3 `DOMNode` methods `contains`, `getRootNode`, `isEqualNode` and `replaceChildren` on every DOM node class, `IntlGregorianCalendar::setDate`/`setDateTime` and `curl_share_init_persistent`. The deltas now have the parameters, and a signature map entry without parameters no longer replaces the parameters known from reflection"," - Keep the type of a variable unknown when it is unknown on some branches and known on others: `$x = null; if ($c) { $x = unknown(); }` (or the same with `try`/`catch`, `switch`, a loop, ...) used to make `$x` exactly `null` because the unknown branch contributed nothing to the merged type, so `PhanTypeMismatchArgument` (and related issues) were reported with certainty for a value that may be anything. The merged type is now `mixed` (resp. `T|mixed`), as the ternary operator already inferred in the same situation. This also makes the issues reported by `--processes N` runs less dependent on which process analyzed the callee, since a callee's inferred return type is only known to the process that analyzed its file"," "," Oct 12 2026, Phan 6.0.10"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Language/Element/FunctionFactory.php","lines":["@@ -251,6 +251,22 @@ public static function functionListFromFunction(","                 }","                 $alternate_function->setUnionType($return_type);","             }","+            if (($map['parameter_name_type_map'] ?? []) === []","+                && $function->getRealParameterList()","+                && Config::get_closest_target_php_version_id() >= \\PHP_VERSION_ID - \\PHP_VERSION_ID % 100","+            ) {","+                // The signature map entry has a return type but no parameters, while reflection says the function or method","+                // has parameters: the entry is incomplete (e.g. a delta generated with return types only). Keep the reflected","+                // parameters instead of replacing them with none, which would report every call as passing too many arguments.","+                // Only when the target PHP version is not older than the running one: the running PHP's reflection may","+                // otherwise carry parameters that the target version does not have yet (e.g. posix_getrlimit()'s $resource,","+                // added in PHP 8.3), and a map entry without parameters may be exactly right for the target version.","+                if (!$alternate_function->getParameterList()) {","+                    $alternate_function->setParameterList($function->getRealParameterList());","+                }","+                $alternate_function->inheritRealParameterDefaults();","+                return $alternate_function;","+            }","             $alternate_function->clearParameterList();"," ","             // Load parameter types if defined"],"addi